summary:
Canon compliant deep dive into Kya. Follows her throughout her life as she embraces her role as a nomadic healer, pioneers healing techniques including a passive form of bloodbending, revives the ancient Air Nomad practice of humanitarian aid trips to help carry on the legacy of her people, and travels the world experiencing everything she possibly can.
─── ⋆⋅ ☾⋅⋆ ───
// 'Book One: Root' — Chapters 1 - 7 //// 'Book Two: Tempest' — First half written, Ch 8-14. New chapters published every Wednesday. After that, stay tuned for the last half of the book and eventually 'Book Three' //

One day Sokka wonders into a tea shop in Ba Sing Se and runs into Zuko of all people, quick to notice he confronts him and Zuko tells him he's turning over a new leaf, Sokka, skeptical as ever, doesn't believe him but goes along with it anyway. Time passes and Sokkas visits become routine, slowly, the two grow on each other.
Or;
Sokka walks into the Jasmine Dragon while Zuko is working. He disrupts his daily life.

Zuko has always been fascinated by the sea and everything in it, ships being a particular interest of his. How they are built, the gears, the types of fuel and how they influence navigation, the hierarchy within a ship and the unique language that the crew uses on the high seas. All this to say, when his father offered him a trip as a high-class passenger on the voyage with the Southern Raiders, he readily accepted, with his luggage in hand and a smile on his face. How lucky he is that his father is so kind!
////////
He first awoke in the wreckage of a ship, surrounded only by snow and sea. Months pass, filled with confusion and fear, until Hakoda finds a nameless little boy with his crew during one of their hunts. Kiran is better than no name at all, isn't it?

When Zuko throws himself directly into the cross fires of battle one too many times Sokka can't handle it any longer.
Or;
Sokka has trauma about losing his loved ones, Zuko is dumb.

“Fire Lord Zuko,” the guard says, gasping for breath between words. Zuko nods twice. “We’ve gotten reports that our food storage in the woods — the large one — was burned by disputants. Nearby guards had asked to call for you immediately.”Zuko sways. Of course something like this would happen as soon as he tries to take a break. The guard notices his hesitation and speaks again.“We think the attacker might be Princess Azula, My Lord.”Zuko sighs.
//
Or, Azula and Zuko meet again, and Azula tries to be a little better.

[ Perhaps he’s scared of admitting his feelings for Zuko, because not too long ago, when he felt the same way about someone else, he lost that person. But maybe he wasn’t scared of his feelings; he was scared of what those feelings could bring. Maybe the idea of falling in love again and again just to end up heartbroken was something his heart couldn’t bear. ]
Or;
Things change after a kiss.
